xnu: mmap of SiliconForest's linuxkpi file descriptors (a dma-buf)

mmap() refused every descriptor that is not a vnode or POSIX shared memory with EINVAL, so
a dma-buf descriptor could not be mapped (a compositor reading a client's buffer, a client
writing one it was handed).

- sf_lfile_ops gains mmap_pages, the question the DRM device nodes already answer through
  sf_cdev_mmap_register(): the physical pages behind a range, their cache mode, and a
  release callback for when the last mapping is gone. sf_lfile_mmap_pages() asks it of a
  descriptor (ENODEV when the registered ops have none).
- mmap(): DTYPE_SFLFILE with MAP_SHARED is mapped through the same device-pager path
  (sf_cdev_mmap_entry, which now takes either a device node or a linux file). MAP_PRIVATE
  is EINVAL; protection beyond the descriptor's open mode is EACCES.

The ops structure grows at its end: a kext built before this registers ops without the
member, so all DRM kexts must be rebuilt with it (they are, from one layer).
UPSTREAM: yes.

